# Demo videos are committed for posterity (su-lou.4 operator decision) but must
# never enter plain git history: a PR demo is ~0.5-5 MB, every re-capture adds
# ANOTHER full copy, and git keeps all of them in every clone forever. git-LFS
# stores a small text pointer in history and the bytes in LFS storage, so the
# videos survive but a clone stays lean.
#
# Requires git-lfs on the machine that COMMITS a video:
#
#   sudo apt install git-lfs && git lfs install     # once per machine
#
# Without it git silently commits the raw bytes while this file claims the blob
# is a pointer -- the one failure mode that is hard to notice and painful to
# undo. `npm run demo:lint` (web/) checks for it before you capture; see
# docs/pr-demo-flow.md.
*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
